From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bakhodirovxz <bohodirovasadbek1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:02:06 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/22] calc, xlsx, engine: keep a calculated file's values on
 open, as Excel does

Every workbook was fully calculated when it opened. Excel doesn't: a file
whose values come from a full calculation (a calcPr without
fullCalcOnLoad, as Excel and gridcraft write it once every formula has a
value) opens with its values as they are. For Excel-saved workbooks that
was most of the open time and of its peak memory.

The XLSX reader reports such a file (`ReadReport::calculated`; not when
spilled values had to be left out), file.open passes it on
(`io::open_bytes_calculated`, `DocState::open`), and `Calc::open` builds
the graph and keeps the values, unless a formula has no value or is
dynamic (volatile, or references only known while calculating): then
everything is calculated, as before. Calculate Now still calculates
everything. Files with fullCalcOnLoad (openpyxl, xlsxwriter) and other
formats are calculated on open as before.
